## **Q4 (a) Basic Operations of Queue (Any Two) + Function Code**

Basic queue operations:
1. **enQueue()** – Insert element at rear  
2. **deQueue()** – Delete element from front  
3. **peek()** – Show front element  
4. **isEmpty(), isFull()** – Validity checks  

### Example Code (Array Queue in C)
```c
#define SIZE 10
int queue[SIZE], front = -1, rear = -1;

void enQueue(int x) {
    if (rear == SIZE - 1)
        printf("Overflow\n");
    else {
        if (front == -1) front = 0;
        queue[++rear] = x;
    }
}

int deQueue() {
    if (front == -1 || front > rear)
        printf("Underflow\n");
    else
        return queue[front++];
}
```

Keep it this short, you score.

