## **Q4 (b) Concept of Circular Queue + enQueue & deQueue**

### **Concept**
Circular queue connects last position back to first.  
No memory waste like linear queue.

```
rear = (rear + 1) % SIZE
front = (front + 1) % SIZE
```

### **Operations**
```c
void enQueue(int x) {
    if ((rear + 1) % SIZE == front)
        printf("Queue Full\n");
    else {
        if (front == -1)
            front = rear = 0;
        else
            rear = (rear + 1) % SIZE;
        queue[rear] = x;
    }
}

int deQueue() {
    int x;
    if (front == -1)
        printf("Queue Empty\n");
    else {
        x = queue[front];
        if (front == rear)
            front = rear = -1;
        else
            front = (front + 1) % SIZE;
        return x;
    }
}
```

